original work notes and a short reflection.","Save work that shows the skill on new material."]},"subject":"Music","success_criteria":["I can use music unit showcase with a specific example from this lesson.","I can identify listening focus and explain why it matters.","I can practise feedback independently on a new prompt.","I can notice reflection needs and correct a likely mistake."],"suspense_builder":null,"teach_steps":[{"check":{"correct_index":1,"explanation":"Showcase compositions with programme notes and a listening focus (hook, loop layers, respectful Australian listening learning). Reflect on composing, technology and protocol awareness. Set a next goal. Supported responses name the element or technique and its effect.","options":["A guess with no artistic reason.","Showcase compositions with programme notes and a listening focus (hook, loop layers, respectful Australian listening learning). Reflect on composing, technology and protocol awareness. Set a next goal.","A comment that only says it looks nice with no element named.","An answer copied without understanding."],"question":"Which choice best shows accurate use of this idea about music unit showcase?","type":"multiple_choice"},"example":"WORKED MODEL\nExample: Focus: ''Listen for the bass loop under the chorus hook.'' Goal: cleaner lyric fit on ti-ti.\n\nTRY FIRST\nWrite a programme note with listening focus and one protocol-aware reflection sentence.\n\nFEEDBACK\nStrong answer: Note guides ears; reflection mentions crediting sources / not inventing restricted content if relevant to learning.","explain":"Showcase compositions with programme notes and a listening focus (hook, loop layers, respectful Australian listening learning). Reflect on composing, technology and protocol awareness. Set a next goal.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS\nThis helps the learner make intentional visual, music, drama or dance choices and name their effect, rather than saying an artwork is simply “nice”. Keep every claim linked to an element or technique.\n\nHOW TO WORK\nRead the worked example and name the elements, techniques or performance choices that carry the idea. Before looking at the correction, make your own attempt using the exact question provided. For movement or instruments, use a clear space, ask an adult to be nearby and stop if anything feels unsafe. You may always describe a choice instead of performing it. One deliberate artistic choice with a named effect is more useful than a longer praise sentence.","icon":"📖","notice":"Ignoring protocol learning in the review. Respect is part of the unit. Name the element or technique and its effect, not just decoration.","title":"Understand and demonstrate","visual":[{"alt":"Composition showcase.","caption":"Guide listening.","svg":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 660 150\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#fff4ea\" stroke=\"#b87445\"/><rect x=\"340\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#e8f5ed\" stroke=\"#297a61\"/><g font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#263948\"><text x=\"28\" y=\"42\">Focus</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"78\">what to hear</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"42\">Feedback</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"78\">stars wish</text></g></svg>"}],"visual_before":[{"episode":{"scenes":[{"bg":"room","lines":[{"text":"I can see the example, but I am not sure which artistic choice matters most.","who":"pip"},{"text":"Name the element, technique or performance choice and the effect it creates before you decide.","who":"juno"},{"text":"I will try the prompt myself, then compare with the feedback.","who":"pip"},{"pause_after":true,"text":"Pause here. Use this example: Example: Focus: ''Listen for the bass loop under the chorus hook.'' Goal: cleaner lyric fit on ti-ti. Then write your own artistic reason.","who":"juno"}]}],"title":"Talk through the first model","transcript":"Pip: I can see the example, but I am not sure which artistic choice matters most.\nJuno: Name the element, technique o